WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.850
Claimant: My 2021 fictional compact SUV was parked in an underground garage during a heavy rainstorm, and floodwater rose around it. Water reached the floorboards, the car won’t start, and the repair estimate is $6,200; there was no collision, fire, or intentional act.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.950
Adjuster: Has a mechanic confirmed whether floodwater caused the car’s failure to start?

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.200
Claimant: I don’t know; the facts don’t say whether a mechanic confirmed the cause.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:41.650
Adjuster: Decision: excluded. The reported floodwater damage is expressly excluded even when the car was parked and the flooding was accidental. Relevant clauses: AUTO-COMP-2. Confidence: 0.98.
